From: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: Test single doorbell hibernation on TB522FU

The Lenovo tablet sees stale MCQ completions after hibernation with
the link in Hibern8. With the link off, UIC link startup instead fails
after firmware restart. The controller capability register indicates
that it also supports single doorbell mode.

Use the legacy queue on this board only when the controller advertises
both modes. Keep Hibern8 as the system sleep link state for that test.
The standard restore callback already restores the legacy request-list
DMA bases. Select the mode before allocating queues in both the saved
and loading kernels. Leave runtime PM and other boards on their
existing settings.

Signed-off-by: Yeye B.B.C. <19569343+yeyebbc@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index 74647e7dfdce6459b9ba66c26d92fe540217dcf8..c4668ba95d2aeb88c792ea5851b1317851a943e0 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -11226,6 +11226,15 @@ int ufshcd_init(struct ufs_hba *hba, void __iomem *mmio_base, unsigned int irq)
 	if (err)
 		goto out_disable;
 
+	/* Test retained Hibern8 using only the legacy DMA lists. */
+	if (hba->mcq_sup && hba->lsdb_sup &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,y900") &&
+	    of_device_is_compatible(hba->dev->of_node, "qcom,sm8750-ufshc")) {
+		hba->mcq_sup = false;
+		hba->spm_lvl = UFS_PM_LVL_3;
+		dev_info(hba->dev, "hibernation test: using SDB at system PM level 3\n");
+	}
+
 	/* Get UFS version supported by the controller */
 	hba->ufs_version = ufshcd_get_ufs_version(hba);
 
